<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shushtar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shushtar is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karun-river">Karun River</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/band-e-kaisar">Band-e Kaisar</a> dam was built across the river near Shushtar using Roman engineering expertise from prisoners captured in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-i">Shapur I</a>'s campaigns. The hydraulic system of Shushtar is regarded as a masterpiece of ancient engineering.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shushtar.jpg" alt="Shushtar" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alireza-Obohat · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shushtar_Historical_Hydraulic_System_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
